  "question": {
    "text": "Half-life of a radio active substance ' $A$ ' is 4 days. The probability that a nucleus will decay in two half-lives is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "1xi31",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{1}{4}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "89qqa",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{3}{4}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "WxeHr",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{1}{2}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "rcvtR",
      "text": "\n1",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "After two half lives $\\frac{1}{4}$ th fraction of nuclei will remain undecayed. Or, $\\frac{3}{4}$ th fraction will decay. Hence, the probability that a nucleus decays in two half lives is $\\frac{3}{4}$.",
    "image": null
  },
